WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.781
An LLM can write code.

00:00:01.781 --> 00:00:03.919
It still can't click a button.

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:06.057
The model is a text engine.

00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:07.482
It has no hands.

00:00:07.482 --> 00:00:10.688
By default, all it can do is generate text.

00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:15.311
Humans don't use computers by writing code.

00:00:15.311 --> 00:00:19.057
We use an interface: a terminal, a website, an app.

00:00:19.057 --> 00:00:22.804
The interface is the part you can see and touch.

00:00:22.804 --> 00:00:24.677
It hides the code underneath.

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:28.194
An LLM needs tools.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.849
It emits a tool call as text.

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:36.157
Something has to parse that text, run the tool, and send the result back.

00:00:36.157 --> 00:00:38.812
The model never runs the tool itself.

00:00:38.812 --> 00:00:40.212
The harness does.

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:41.845
That loop is the harness.

00:00:44.045 --> 00:00:52.184
A harness is five things: the tools, the syntax for calling them, a parser, a result channel, and a list of what's available.

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:54.307
Miss one and the loop breaks.

00:00:56.307 --> 00:00:58.569
Claude Code is kind of a harness.

00:00:58.569 --> 00:01:01.801
It bakes the interface and the harness into one app.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.417
The interface is for you.

00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:05.356
The harness is for the model.

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:11.496
Think of a kitchen: the tools are pots and pans, and a good harness lets you bring your own.

00:01:13.696 --> 00:01:16.524
An agent is an LLM plus a harness.

00:01:16.524 --> 00:01:18.291
The model is the chef.

00:01:18.291 --> 00:01:20.058
The harness is the kitchen.

00:01:20.058 --> 00:01:25.006
And T3 Code is the restaurant that lets you bring whatever kitchen you want.

00:01:25.006 --> 00:01:26.773
That is the whole trick.
